{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unbeatable-unlit-gadwall","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## What\n\nCut the user-visible message strings over: `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py:556,597,600,614` (and the\ndocstrings at 532,564,568) and `src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py:34,58`\n(`COMPLETION_REMEDIATION_GUIDANCE`, `INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE_REMEDIATION`).\n\n## Note on INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE_REMEDIATION\n\nIts text draws the distinction that motivated this tag name: record code proof as an UNTAGGED\ncomment; do NOT tag code-verifiable criteria. Re-word it against `[non-codebase]` and the\ninstruction becomes self-reinforcing rather than merely prohibitive — a test path is obviously\nnot \"non-codebase\".\n\n## Asserting tests to update\n\n`tests/unit/test_attested_close_guard.py:55`,\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ac_checkbox_precheck.py:80`,\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ac_checkbox_precheck_heldout.py:235`,\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py:178`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All six message/remediation strings name `[non-codebase]`.\n- [ ] The four asserting tests are updated and pass.\n- [ ] A close blocked by the laundering guard and one blocked by the provenance guard both\n      produce messages naming the new tag, proved end-to-end.","id":"2b15-9d27-90b1-4e7a","parent_id":"6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S6 — cut close-guard and remediation strings over to [non-codebase]"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787186009756219001,"uuid":"aeb0e24c-3477-4a75-b109-2a2d07af3db1"}